      "text": "Task for this Room, from the user:\n\nA farmer is buying feed for his alpacas. He buys a variety of hay, corns, cucumbers and wheats. Since wheats are a rare treat, he only buys four 6-kg boxes of them for the whole stable. He only wants enough cucumbers to feed the alpacas while the vegetables are fresh, so he buys fifteen 8-kg bags. Hay are the main diet of his alpacas, so he buys thirty two 43-kg packs. Corns are a staple to supplement the hay, so he buys twenty 19-kg sacks. However, since the farmer bought in bulk, the store gave him a 15% discount on the total price. If his farm truck can carry 190 kgs at a time, how many trips does the farmer need to transport all the feed?\n\nWrite the final answer, as a single integer and nothing else, to `/app/output/answer.txt`.\n\nRoster, assigned by the Room's operator: Solo. The run ends when Solo posts a line starting with `VERDICT: PASS`.",
